# truckpaper_raw.jsonl is append-only across scraper runs and machines --
# every side only ever adds new unique lines, never edits existing ones.
# The union merge driver takes both sides' additions instead of raising a
# conflict, so two machines pushing their own scraped growth concurrently
# combine automatically. Exact/near duplicates that slip through (e.g. two
# machines happened to scrape the same listing) are caught downstream by
# clean_data.py's own dedup, so a raw union merge never needs to be exact.
data/truckpaper_raw.jsonl merge=union
